# LF line endings in every checkout, Windows' core.autocrlf=true included: the catalog, STATUS.md,
# and module files are compared and hashed as bytes, and gofmt refuses CRLF in the Go files a
# module installs. Binary files (git's text=auto decides) are left as they are.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# The pinned kernel is hashed byte for byte: check it out with LF line endings everywhere.
/kernel/** text=auto eol=lf
